{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the control helper's runner selection, answering 30b5d71d. Queued; nothing changes in the 7c0e8181 branch.\n\n1. The repair. scripts/control.mjs picks `node --test` whenever the package's test script has a `node --test` clause (scripts/control.mjs:60-70). In packages/cli the script runs both runners, so a Vitest file is handed to Node. The repair selects by the requested file: if the file is named by the script's `node --test` clause, Node runs it; otherwise Vitest does. The helper also keeps the baseline child's stderr in the capture, so an inconclusive row says why. One file, two tests (a package with both runners; a package with one), no other change.\n\n2. Where it goes. Fold the repair into the next head that touches scripts/control.mjs or docs/testing.md. If none comes before J4 lands, it is a standalone one-file head after J4, filed by the planner then. It is not a child of 7c0e8181 and does not enter its gate.\n\n3. The controls. control-unique-entry-1 stays in the 7c0e8181 note as an inconclusive row with its cause (runner mis-selected), and control-unique-entry-2, the explicit Vitest invocation, is the paired control the ruling of 2a308f5d and the request's witness need. No exception-type claim is made from the first run.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}